<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Purdil Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1830</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Purdil Khan was the eldest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardar">Sardars</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barakzai-dynasty">Barakzai</a> brothers who took Kandahar after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani Empire</a> broke up in 1818. A half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dost-mohammad-khan">Dost Mohammad Khan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>, he led the brothers' joint rule of the principality until his death in 1830, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kohandil-khan">Kohandil Khan</a> succeeded him at its head.</p></div>
